  "worked_solution": "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{cos}^{2}\u2061t)\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-5)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{\u2033}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2033}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\ -6({cos}^{2}\u2061t-{sin}^{2}\u2061t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}^{\u2033}(\\pi )$ by substituting $t=\\pi $ into the above:\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2033}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\pi  \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\pi  \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-(-1)-0 \\\\ -6\\cdot 1 \\\\ -4\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
